<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hashid</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hashid are one of the two great tribal confederations of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakil">Bakil</a>, living in the highlands north of Sanaa. Long a main military support of the Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a>, they are known for their cohesion, and their paramount sheikhs of the al-Ahmar family became leading figures in the Yemen Arab Republic and in unified Yemen after 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hashid.jpg" alt="Hashid" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ibrahem Qasim · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheikh_sadiq_al-ahmar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
